###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Relative computational costs (graphene GAP 340, amorphous GAP 380 relative to Tersoff) are not absolute timings. Tersoff, REBO, AIREBO, AIREBO-Morse, LCBOP, ReaxFF and DFTB errors are not MLIPs and are not encoded.
# - The amorphous-carbon GAP of Ref. 24 is linked to the label 'GAP-17 amorphous carbon'; the paper calls it 'the recently published GAP model for the amorphous phase'.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
